Z||000002||Greg Piet||01-21-2001||04:25 PM||||Any car show that spends an entire episode showing you how to mop up spilled oil, and how to use double sticky tape makes me think twice about buying something that they worked on.  Now they have so many things in their new shop it is too far removed from the general car person.  <P>The last episode I saw they were showing people how to attach on lens covers/bugguard/tonneau cover on a pickup truck.  (What a fricking waste of a lift, complete air tool collection)...  And why dont they have a press, but they have so many other things(like the lift)(they said they had to take something to a machine shop to press something in/out)??????   <P>The show before was showing how to weld tube steel together to make a tool tray on wheels...<P>What happened to showing how to put on blowers, or selecting the right jetting for your carb, hell even something as trivial as how to properly set your float in the carb or adjusting your points,  or a more modern thing like selecting the right MSD system?<P>Or even tricks for seperating ball joints...<BR>Something besides making your truck look like a girlie girlie truck(no offense ladies, but its a truck!).<P>I used to enjoy their show, when it really was more of a shadetree mechanic show, at least it had the potential to prove useful to the average joe.<P>ok im done complaining.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR>Bring it to the track.<BR>Lets see if all those mods really helped!||||reg||1
